    "description": "Enter The Earth / Making Memories\nNatural Mineral and Fossil Specimen Collection\nGeology Study Lot, Late 20th to Early 21st Century\nThis comprehensive geological collection features a diverse array of natural mineral specimens, fossils, and hand-carved gemstones. The lot is anchored by a 18-compartment organizer containing various rough stones including rose quartz, amethyst, jasper, and apatite, accompanied by a descriptive insert regarding Coprolite (fossilized dung). Complementing the boxed set are several larger individual display pieces and professional carvings from international sources.\nPolished Pyrite sphere with \"Made in Peru\" label featuring natural vuggy texture\nPolished Orthoceras cephalopod fossil specimen in black matrix\nAmethyst geode with iridescent gold-tone titanium-treated coating\nFour hand-carved stone animal figurines: Kambaba, Picture Jasper (Oregon), and Tigereye (South Africa)\nClear plastic organizer box with approximately 18 varieties of rough and tumbled mineral specimens\nCondition:\nVery good overall condition. Mineral specimens are in their natural rough or polished states as intended. The pyrite sphere and geode are intact with no structural cracks. The carved animals are housed in original protective plastic cases; cases show minor surface scuffing but remain functional. The main organizer box is complete and latches securely, though the lid shows typical light storage wear.",
